comment begin
    Imports that name nothing.

    This program does not compile. An import names one file, relative to the file that wrote
    it, and the file has to be there and has to be Profi-C.

    An import that points at an absolute path is a warning rather than an error: it is correct
    on the machine that wrote it and nowhere else. That case is not shown here, because a
    warning is not what this folder records.
end comment

import "nowhere.pc";
import "../runtime/notes.txt";
import "sideways/Missing.pc";

global model Program
    function Main()
        Console.WriteLine("never reached");
    end function
end model
